---
description: "Hard boundaries — no destructive git or database actions without explicit sign-off"
alwaysApply: true
---

These are boundaries, not preferences. Never do the following without asking first and getting an explicit yes:

- No `git push --force`, no rewriting history, no deleting branches, no direct commits/pushes to `main`.
- No `DROP`, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`, or destructive `ALTER` on any database, and no data-losing migration, even in a "safe" environment — ask first, every time.
- No editing of `.env`, secrets, CI/CD configs, or GitHub repo settings unless the task explicitly requires it and I've confirmed.
- If a task seems to require any of the above to succeed, stop and explain why instead of finding a workaround.
